      shortDescription: 'An electronically controlled valve delivering precise pulses of atomized fuel into the intake port or combustion chamber.',
      fullDescription: 'A fuel injector is a precision electromechanical valve controlled by the ECU. When energized, it opens for a precisely calculated duration and sprays a fine mist of fuel at high pressure. Modern injectors can operate thousands of times per minute with extreme accuracy.',
      howItWorks: ['Fuel supplied under pressure (3-6 bar petrol, 150-350 bar GDI) to the fuel rail.','ECU calculates required fuel and sends electrical signal to the injector solenoid.','Solenoid energizes, opening the needle valve.','Pressurized fuel atomizes through nozzle orifices.','ECU cuts signal — spring closes needle valve.'],
